.TH ICLOUD-SYNC 1 "2026" "icloud-sync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
icloud-sync \- two-way iCloud Drive synchronization for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B icloud-sync
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B icloud-sync
keeps a local folder in two-way sync with iCloud Drive. It drives
.BR rclone (1)
(bisync with the iclouddrive backend) and adds a background service that
reacts to local changes through inotify, a lightweight check for remote
changes, safety checks against mass deletion, automatic recovery, Apple
login renewal reminders and a system tray icon.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Guided configuration: rclone, Apple login, first sync, background service.
.TP
.B status
Show the synchronization state.
.TP
.BR sync " [" \-\-dry\-run "] [" \-\-force ]
Synchronize now.
.TP
.BR resync " [" \-\-prefer " newer|local|icloud]"
Realign both sides from scratch; nothing is deleted.
.TP
.BR login " [" \-\-gui "] [" \-\-new\-password "] [" \-\-reset ]
Authenticate the Apple ID again (needed about every 30 days).
.B \-\-gui
opens a window instead of asking in the terminal.
.TP
.BR pause ", " resume
Suspend and resume automatic synchronization.
.TP
.BR enable ", " disable ", " restart
Manage the background service and the tray icon.
.TP
.B tray
Run the system tray icon (needs PyQt6).
.TP
.BR skipped " [" \-\-retry ]
List items iCloud does not let rclone download.
.TP
.BR log " [" \-n " N] [" \-\-error ]
Show recent activity.
.TP
.B doctor
Run a full diagnostic.
.TP
.B install\-rclone
Install or update the official rclone binary in ~/.local/bin.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/icloud-sync/config.toml
Configuration (commented).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/icloud-sync/
State and logs.
